    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "fbbdf308-bc9c-386e-b6d6-2b718f880434",
                "word": "athanor",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "0ec113ca-3718-42ef-9322-447dbfe424e0",
                        "entry_id": "fbbdf308-bc9c-386e-b6d6-2b718f880434",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "athanors"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "84f8af0d-ed87-3dcf-9730-48618d313b32",
                        "entry_id": "fbbdf308-bc9c-386e-b6d6-2b718f880434",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A furnace or stove designed and used to maintain uniform heat, primarily used by alchemists."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3b71dd35-f1f3-4e1f-ac28-5f4212be4d52",
                                "sense_id": "84f8af0d-ed87-3dcf-9730-48618d313b32",
                                "text": "You may also be inſtructed, That when you are diſtilling of Aqua fort. and that the Coals in the Athanor are almoſt gone out (which happens hardly in 10 or 11 hours) then lift up the Cover from the Athanor, make it full again with Coals and cover it, elſe the Fire will go out, and all will be cold, as Oportunity it ſelf will teach thee and make thee to remember."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "39fb42eb-02b5-4aa5-99ca-ffd4495b02be",
                                "sense_id": "84f8af0d-ed87-3dcf-9730-48618d313b32",
                                "text": "The Furnace call'd an Athanor, was invented to keep a conſtant Heat for Fourteen Days, a Month, Twelve Months, or more, as ſome Chymical Operations require, which may be augmented or decreaſed, by opening or ſhutting the Regiſters, as you pleaſe, and according to the Magnitude of the Tower, requires no Attendance above once in twenty four, fourty eight, or one hundred Hours."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fe2c8c67-f1ae-45cb-b322-a54206e5511d",
                                "sense_id": "84f8af0d-ed87-3dcf-9730-48618d313b32",
                                "text": "The long and tedious operations of the ancient chemists rendered it a desirable requisite, that their fires should be constantly supplied with fuel in proportion to the consumption. The athanor furnace was peculiarly adapted to this purpose."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "512bc815-2ad1-4ede-81ec-163a61a02a5a",
                                "sense_id": "84f8af0d-ed87-3dcf-9730-48618d313b32",
                                "text": "The Magus should not, therefore, live exclusively in his laboratory, amidst his Athanor, his elixirs, and his pantacles. […] A magical operation should invariably be followed by a rest of equal duration and an analogous diversion, but one contrary in its object."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6540fe22-0ecf-4b0d-9755-0b90b4ad3abe",
                                "sense_id": "84f8af0d-ed87-3dcf-9730-48618d313b32",
                                "text": "Without sincere prayer nothing permanent or divine could be accomplished. Hence while the Operation of the Mass is in progress, and the fire in the Athanor becomes more intense, an enthusiastic invocation, either astral or audible, should be recited."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9d77931e-c3df-4892-a38b-785444b75239",
                                "sense_id": "84f8af0d-ed87-3dcf-9730-48618d313b32",
                                "text": "Incomprehensible additions and deletions made by dazed scribes suffering from poor candlelight, weak from unbalanced diets, given to sudden attacks of vertigo as they struggled through the night with pen and paper in vaulted medieval laboratories, hopelessly trying to record the great doctor's mutterings, his whispered arcane wisdom that rose with the fumes spiraling up from his vast array of pelicans and alembics, crucibles and athanors."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fdf50196-8818-49aa-9bcd-f6412969e009",
                        "source_entry_id": "fbbdf308-bc9c-386e-b6d6-2b718f880434",
                        "source_sense_id": "84f8af0d-ed87-3dcf-9730-48618d313b32",
                        "source_sense_description": "furnace or stove designed and used to maintain uniform heat, primarily used by alchemists",
                        "target_lang_word": "athanor",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "athanor",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1aa3e075-bf8b-3212-b811-7e98569acfe8",
                                        "entry_id": "1a2a92e2-2c6b-321d-a3e7-79bda70409b0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Four d’alchimiste, à combustion très lente."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ed257790-d656-4b58-969a-139d0e223d61",
                                                "sense_id": "1aa3e075-bf8b-3212-b811-7e98569acfe8",
                                                "text": "Mais là aussi une immense et harassante liberté lui restait encore : il pouvait à son gré s’en tenir à cette décision ou y renoncer, faire le geste qui termine tout ou au contraire accepter cette mors ignea guère différente de l’agonie d’un alchimiste enflammant par mégarde sa longue robe aux braises de son athanor."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44114e79-777c-4f9e-b051-7e6a37997bf3",
                                                "sense_id": "1aa3e075-bf8b-3212-b811-7e98569acfe8",
                                                "text": "Oui, la chambre à four, avec ses chevrons, ses murs nus et sa suie séculaire, c’était l’athanor où le feu se transformait en principe de vie ; voilà pourquoi je m’y réfugiais, pour y renifler dix siècles de ce vrai confort, qu’on n’a d’ailleurs jamais remplacé, et pour y mijoter les expériences gustatives personnelles, les seules valables."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b80b6a03-461f-40e9-b03a-4c51a9b56e6e",
                                                "sense_id": "1aa3e075-bf8b-3212-b811-7e98569acfe8",
                                                "text": "L'étuve abandonnée était vraiment une chambre magique; la grande flamme sensuelle transmutait tout comme celle de l'athanor alchimique et valait qu'on risquât celle des bûchers."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
